Q: How to fix Package source mapping is off in Visual Studio 2022? A: <p>Package Manager UI: <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/nuget/consume-packages/nuget-visual-studio-options#package-source-mapping" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Accessing NuGet Options</a></p>
<ul>
<li>Press the settings (gear) icon in the Package Manager UI toolbar.</li>
<li>Select a package from the list</li>
<li>Click <strong>Configure</strong> (link directly next to the &quot;Package source mapping is off&quot; warning banner)</li>
<li>Package Source Mappings Options</li>
<li>Click Add <a href="https://i.sstatic.net/624JeNBM.jpg" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/624JeNBM.jpg" alt="Add button" /></a></li>
<li>Select <code>nuget.org</code></li>
<li>Package pattern: <code>*</code></li>
<li>Add <a href="https://i.sstatic.net/3YRq2rlD.jpg" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/3YRq2rlD.jpg" alt="Add" /></a></li>
<li>OK</li>
</ul>
<p>After <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/nuget/consume-packages/package-source-mapping#enabling-package-source-mapping" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Enabling Package Source Mapping</a>
your <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/nuget/reference/nuget-config-file" rel="nofollow noreferrer">nuget.config</a> looks:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;utf-8&quot;?&gt;
&lt;configuration&gt;
  &lt;packageSources&gt;
    &lt;clear /&gt;
    &lt;add key=&quot;nuget.org&quot; value=&quot;https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;/packageSources&gt;

  &lt;packageSourceMapping&gt;
    &lt;!-- Map all packages to nuget.org --&gt;
    &lt;packageSource key=&quot;nuget.org&quot;&gt;
      &lt;package pattern=&quot;*&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;/packageSource&gt;
  &lt;/packageSourceMapping&gt;
&lt;/configuration&gt;
</code></pre>

